<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαφρ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>frothy,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλαγος</span> Sch.BT <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύσματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					9.564
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρυφαῖος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Heraclid.
			</span></i>
			
				Tarent.
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>, who cites <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>de Arte</u>
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Frr.</u>
				236
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				312
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαφρον ὄμμ᾽ ἔχων</span>
			(of Odysseus) in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				711
			</span></i> (lyr.), acc. to Sch.; <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> explains by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μὴ
			φανερόν,</span> also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρύφιον καὶ
				ὕπουλον,</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑγρασίαν
				ἔχον ἐμφερῆ ἀφρῷ</span> (i.e. <i>blear</i>-eyed in <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> l.c.). [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαφρον</span> codd. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕποφρος </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ον</span>) codd.<i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> this sense hardly fits, and Littré accepts
			Schneider's cj. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόφορον</span> 'pierced
			with ducts'.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
